---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { getSitePage, REVIEWED_DATE, REVIEWED_ISO } from "../data/sitePages";

const page = getSitePage("/declarations/");
---

<BaseLayout
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  alternateMd="/declarations/index.md"
  pageType="WebPage"
  dateModified={REVIEWED_ISO}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Declarations" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Documents and declarations</h1>
      <p class="small">Last reviewed: {REVIEWED_DATE}</p>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--ink-2)">
        A supplier that cannot say what it does not hold is difficult to verify. This page lists the documents we can
        request or provide, what each document proves, what it does not prove, and the claims we do not make.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What this page covers</h2>
      <p>
        The table is a guide to documents for a quotation, a first order or a compliance file. Availability depends
        on the material, the producer and the shipment. We will tell you before payment if a document cannot be
        obtained, whose name is on it and whether it applies to the exact grade or batch you are buying.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Documents you can request</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Document</th><th scope="col">What it proves</th><th scope="col">What it does not prove</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Business licence copy</td><td>The registered name, USCC and status of {site.company.legalNameEn}</td><td>That we own a factory, hold a certification or have capacity for a particular order</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Material data sheet</td><td>The producer's stated construction, properties and recommended use for a named grade</td><td>That the finished label on your container will perform in your conditions, or that a food-contact use is approved</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Batch record extract</td><td>The material grade, lot or batch, quantity and production or inspection fields the producer records</td><td>A full factory audit, an independent test or a guarantee that every carton behaves identically</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Test report, if the producer supplies one</td><td>That a sample was tested to a named method under the conditions stated in that report</td><td>A product certification, a certificate in our name or proof that every production batch meets the same result</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Safety data sheet (SDS), where applicable</td><td>The producer's hazard, handling and transport information for a chemical product</td><td>Food-contact approval, regulatory clearance for your label or a statement that a material is suitable for every use</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Origin and shipment information</td><td>The origin and commercial-invoice data stated for a particular shipment, including the HS code used</td><td>A binding customs classification ruling, a change of origin or a guarantee of duty treatment in the destination country</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>3. Tested to a method is not certified</h2>
      <p>
        A report may say that a material was tested to a named method, for example an ISO or ASTM method. That is a
        statement about the sample and test conditions; it is not a product certification and it is not our test. We
        do not hold an ISO 9001 certificate, a CE mark for a label, an FSC chain-of-custody certificate, a GS1
        certification, a factory audit or a food-contact certification. If your file needs one of those, tell us
        before the quotation so we can say whether the producer can provide a document in its own name. We will not
        manufacture a certificate to win an order.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Batch traceability fields</h2>
      <p>
        Where the producer records them, a batch or lot reference can connect your order to a material grade,
        production date, quantity and inspection result. Useful fields include the order or quotation number, the
        material and adhesive grade, the producer's lot number, the production or inspection date, the packed quantity
        and any result recorded for that run. Availability differs by material and producer, so we do not claim that
        every field exists for every job. If traceability is a condition of your purchase, put the required fields in
        the quotation before the order is confirmed.
      </p>

      <h2 id="photography">5. Photography and customer privacy</h2>
      <p>
        We do not publish photographs of printed work, customer artwork or finished packaging without written
        permission. That is a privacy rule, not a claim that the work does not exist. Product visuals on this site are
        <strong>industrial schematics</strong>, not photographs of customer jobs, and they are not AI-generated
        product photographs. They are drawings of formats and construction, labelled as such wherever they appear.
        Written permission can support a disclosed case study; without it, the illustration is the honest
        alternative.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Document request process and timing</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Document request`}>{site.email}</a> with the subject
        <strong>Document request</strong>, the quotation or order reference, the document you need, the market and
        the intended use. We acknowledge a document request within 2 business days and tell you whether it is held by
        us, must be requested from the producer, or is not available. A producer or laboratory reply can take longer,
        and we will not promise a date that depends on a third party without saying so.
      </p>

      <h2>7. How to verify us</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Search the USCC <strong>{site.company.uscc}</strong> in China's National Enterprise Credit Information Publicity System (<a href="https://www.gsxt.gov.cn/index.html" rel="noopener">gsxt.gov.cn</a>).</li>
        <li>Check the D-U-N-S number <strong>{site.company.duns}</strong> through Dun &amp; Bradstreet (<a href="https://www.dnb.com/duns-number/lookup.html" rel="noopener">dnb.com</a>).</li>
        <li>Confirm that the invoice is issued in the name of {site.company.legalNameEn} and that banking details appear only on that invoice.</li>
        <li>Compare the document's company name, grade and batch reference with the quotation and the goods.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>8. What we do not claim</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not own a printing factory. We specify, coordinate and quality-check work produced by partner presses in China.</li>
        <li>We do not hold ISO 9001, CE, FSC, GS1, food-contact or social-compliance certifications for the labels we sell.</li>
        <li>We do not claim FDA approval, a factory audit or a test result that we cannot produce on request.</li>
        <li>We do not publish customer names, logos or photographs without written permission.</li>
        <li>We do not provide legal advice, a customs classification ruling or a guarantee that a marketplace or authority will accept a label.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. What this means for a first order</h2>
      <p>
        We can specify a material, check artwork, request producer documents, place the job, inspect output against
        the approved proof and arrange shipment. We cannot turn a trading company into a testing laboratory or a law
        firm. If your compliance process needs a document that does not exist, the honest answer is “not available”,
        and it is better to hear that before the deposit than to receive a PDF that does not survive verification.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        Related policies: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> ·
        <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> · <a href="/refund-policy/">Returns</a> ·
        <a href="/shipping-delivery/">Shipping</a> · <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial standards</a> ·
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> · <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a> ·
        <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility</a> ·
        <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
